  [1mThe short version of what happened to your request:[0m you asked for a notifications system; what the spec describes is
  [1mdue dates on tasks, surfaced in the list on load[0m. That's not me trimming scope unilaterally — it follows from your two
  answers. Single-user means you are the only one changing your tasks, so change notifications would mostly report your
  own edits back to you. And a page can't reach you when it's closed without the server you ruled out. The remaining
  honest version of "notify me about tasks I care about" is an [38;5;153mOverdue (3)[39m heading you can't miss when you open the app.

  The spec records that reasoning in a "How This Scope Was Reached" section, deliberately — so the dropped
  infrastructure doesn't quietly creep back in during implementation.

